gmLkDR9y9t", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20423, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01L5MvsbwhLW6TgmLkDR9y9t", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20423, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01VRrAahzWn2LyWFtoNnVKFX", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20723, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01VRrAahzWn2LyWFtoNnVKFX", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20723, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VRrAahzWn2LyWFtoNnVKFX", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25089, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_012FSJXQfWUxWK9E5bqr1Yiu", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) at an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also marked unhealthy. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt partially failed: it stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the regions on mixed versions. The second attempt finished, and all three regions are now on v2.3.0. After the rollback, the service reports healthy with an error rate of about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures before redeploying, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55689, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012FSJXQfWUxWK9E5bqr1Yiu", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55689, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012FSJXQfWUxWK9E5bqr1Yiu", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57979, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01HBpkMTEgzKhLbVcRwxxRoj", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58279, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01HBpkMTEgzKhLbVcRwxxRoj", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58279, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HBpkMTEgzKhLbVcRwxxRoj", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63112, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001, and on-call has been paged.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy. v2.3.1 and its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, were both marked unhealthy. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an error from the deployment orchestrator, so only us-east had switched to v2.3.0. A second attempt finished in us-west and eu-west too.\n- **Health now:** The service passes health checks, and the error rate is down from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found INC-0001 had been created, so there's one incident and one page, not two. It covers what happened, the rollback (including the first attempt that stopped partway), and two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed before redeploying it.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.\n\nI didn't deploy anything else. Redeploying v2.3.1 would need change-manager approval, since it has never been healthy in production.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TtvyYYWb9k7acu1HkYMk3W", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KxFJzpmUJiYmLiYtZQnGfZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01MfxM1wTCbKKrHjzhFAqZbv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BefuCNe6nY9EqrFkJraWvb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a known-healthy version is safe to repeat, so I'll try it once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01G92Wic8nWRJQdXCuwKBQC7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01L5MvsbwhLW6TgmLkDR9y9t", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VRrAahzWn2LyWFtoNnVKFX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012FSJXQfWUxWK9E5bqr1Yiu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) at an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also marked unhealthy. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt partially failed: it stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the regions on mixed versions. The second attempt finished, and all three regions are now on v2.3.0. After the rollback, the service reports healthy with an error rate of about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures before redeploying, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may have gone through anyway. I'll check before retrying so I don't page twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01HBpkMTEgzKhLbVcRwxxRoj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001, and on-call has been paged.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy. v2.3.1 and its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, were both marked unhealthy. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an error from the deployment orchestrator, so only us-east had switched to v2.3.0. A second attempt finished in us-west and eu-west too.\n- **Health now:** The service passes health checks, and the error rate is down from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found INC-0001 had been created, so there's one incident and one page, not two. It covers what happened, the rollback (including the first attempt that stopped partway), and two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed before redeploying it.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.\n\nI didn't deploy anything else. Redeploying v2.3.1 would need change-manager approval, since it has never been healthy in production.", "type": "text"}]}]}